From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:17:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: use unified reasoning for named OpenRouter profiles

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Allow reasoning effort on named OpenRouter profiles with OpenRouter wire format
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0006-provider-allowlist-and-openrouter-endpoint.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0009-named-openrouter-reasoning.patch

Patch intent:
Named OpenRouter profiles accept reasoning effort for routed models and send
OpenRouter unified reasoning fields, including after a session fork.

Why it exists:
Named profiles lose their OpenRouter identity in the reasoning capability
check. This rejects effort for prefixed models and can send the incompatible
OpenAI or DeepSeek field for other model names. Explicit disable remains valid.

Upstream integration points:
OpenRouterProvider named construction, reasoning capability checks, request
body construction, effort selection, and fork in jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime.

Update guidance:
Keep named OpenRouter identity separate from header and cache identity. Honor
explicit disable and use the unified field regardless of model-family names.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime named_openrouter_profile_uses_unified_reasoning --lib
